================================================================================
S1. DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

"Software"
    The QPT source code, model architecture, documented training
    procedures, inference code, configuration files, and all associated
    documentation made available under this License.

"Model"
    Any artificial intelligence or machine learning model trained using the
    Software, in whole or in part, including fine-tuned, distilled, or
    derived variants.

"Training Phase"
    The computational process by which a Model is produced, including data
    preprocessing, gradient updates, and evaluation during training.

"Inference Phase"
    The process by which a trained Model generates outputs in response to
    inputs, whether deployed locally, on-premises, or via a network service.

"Dataset"
    Any collection of data used as input to the Training Phase. Datasets used
    with or produced alongside the Software are governed by S6 of this License.

"Derivative Work"
    Any work that is based on or incorporates the Software, including
    modifications, adaptations, translations, or extensions.

"Commercial Use"
    Any use of the Software, a Model trained using the Software, or a
    Derivative Work, in a product or service for which a fee is charged, or
    that contributes to revenue generation, including indirect monetization
    through advertising, subscriptions, or data collection. Commercial Use
    also includes using the Software to train a Model that is subsequently
    used commercially, even if the Software itself is not distributed.

"Large Commercial User"
    Any legal entity whose Annual Gross Revenue attributable to a product or
    service that incorporates or relies upon the Software, a Model trained
    using the Software, or a Derivative Work, exceeds USD $5,000,000 --
    adjusted for inflation as measured by the Consumer Price Index (CPI) of
    the jurisdiction where the entity is incorporated or primarily operates,
    with 2026 as the base year. If no local equivalent index exists, the U.S.
    Bureau of Labor Statistics CPI-U shall apply.

"R&D Tax Reduction"
    A formal fiscal benefit under applicable national law by which a legal
    entity reduces its tax liability by reason of qualifying research and
    development expenditure made to or on behalf of QPT. To satisfy the
    obligations in S5, the expenditure must: (a) be directed to activities
    that directly benefit the QPT-LLM project; (b) be documented in writing;
    and (c) be verifiable by QPT upon request.

"Hybrid Algorithm"
    Any algorithm developed as part of the QPT-LLM project that combines
    techniques from two or more distinct fields (e.g., quantum computing and
    machine learning,photonic computing and machine learning , thermodinamic computing and
    machine learning) and constitutes a novel, non-obvious technical
    contribution.

"QPT"
    Quantum Photonic Thermodinamic Large Language Model, the originating organization and licensor
    of the Software.

	For the purposes of this License, “QPT” refers to the research group, project, or organization responsible for the development, maintenance, and stewardship of the QPT-LLM and QPT-B3-LLM  Software and its associated research. At the time of publication of this License, QPT is directed and administered by Victor Daniel Arango Sohm, who acts as the person responsible for the project and as the holder of the rights associated with QPT-LLM, unless expressly stated otherwise.

	At the time of publication of this License, QPT operates as a research group or project and is not necessarily constituted as a separate legal entity. If QPT subsequently becomes incorporated as a company, foundation, nonprofit organization, or other legal entity, the rights and responsibilities associated with QPT under this License may be transferred to or exercised by such successor entity, as formally determined by Victor Daniel Arango Sohm or the applicable copyright holder.

	The term “QPT”, by itself, does not constitute a representation that a company, foundation, nonprofit organization, or other legal entity currently exists under that name.

"QPT-LLM"
    Quantum Photonic Thermodinamic Large Language Model, the original product of QPT and the center of the reaserch.

"Contribution"

    Any source code, documentation, data, money, or other material submitted to QPT
    for inclusion in the Software or Hardware.

"Significant Contribution"

A contribution is deemed significant when an individual, institution, corporation, university, or other entity provides at least ten percent (10%) of the total measurable effort required to design, develop, implement, validate, or substantially advance a protected intellectual creation, software, algorithm, invention, or research output to date.To determine and quantify an entity's exact contribution value, stakeholders must apply the calculation methodology specified in the project's Scoring_Framework_Roadmap.md documentation.  

