  (d) any sublicense granted to a third party is on terms no less restrictive
      than this License.

You may not sublicense the Software in a manner that would allow a third party
to use it without attribution obligations or share-alike requirements.


================================================================================
S5. COMMERCIAL USE
================================================================================

5.1  Permitted Commercial Use

     Commercial Use of the Software is permitted subject to this section.
     Any entity engaging in Commercial Use must:

       (a) comply with all attribution and share-alike conditions in S3;
       (b) not misrepresent the origin or nature of the Software;
       (c) include a disclosure in product documentation or terms of service
           stating that the product incorporates QPT.

5.2  Large Commercial User Obligation

     A Large Commercial User must, on an annual basis, satisfy at least one
     of the following obligations:

       (a) make a direct monetary donation to QPT; or
       (b) apply an R&D Tax Reduction under applicable national law, structured
           so that the economic benefit flows to or is credited to QPT.

     The economic value of the donation or R&D Tax Reduction must be
     proportional to the revenue generated from the product or service that
     incorporates the Software. QPT will publish a contribution schedule
     specifying suggested amounts based on revenue tiers.

     This obligation applies equally to Commercial Use in the Training Phase
     (i.e., using the Software to train a Model that is subsequently used
     commercially, even if the Software itself is not redistributed).

     The USD $5,000,000 threshold and all monetary amounts in this License
     are denominated in United States Dollars as of 2026 and adjusted
     annually using the applicable CPI as described in S1.


================================================================================
S6. DATASETS
================================================================================

Datasets used in the Training Phase of a Model are NOT covered by this
License. Each dataset must be governed by its own license, appropriate to its
content and provenance.

If you create a new dataset in connection with the Software or a Model trained
using the Software, and you distribute or publish that dataset, you must:

  (a) publish the dataset under a separate, clearly specified license
      (e.g., CC BY 4.0, CC BY-SA 4.0, or an equivalent open data license);
  (b) include a dataset card or equivalent documentation describing the
      dataset's contents, provenance, collection methodology, and any known
      limitations or biases;
  (c) not impose on the dataset license any terms that conflict with this
      License or that would prevent recipients from using the dataset with
      the Software.

QPT makes no representations regarding the licensing of datasets used
internally. Third-party datasets referenced in QPT documentation are subject
to their respective licenses.


